    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "you say it's \"a matter of whether you prioritize\" one or the other, but when you look at the actual data from that decade, isn't it pretty much a fact that deregulation was the main driver for the growth we saw? like, wouldn't the \"consensus\" be that the growth was the successful part, and the inequality was just a side effect?",
